1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:01,994
A customer taps one button,

2
00:00:01,994 --> 00:00:04,153
and a second later the products appear.

3
00:00:04,153 --> 00:00:06,367
But what really happened in that second?

4
00:00:06,917 --> 00:00:07,552
Somewhere,

5
00:00:07,552 --> 00:00:09,013
a page was handed over,

6
00:00:09,013 --> 00:00:10,346
a question was asked,

7
00:00:10,346 --> 00:00:11,363
a file was read,

8
00:00:11,363 --> 00:00:12,887
and an answer came back.

9
00:00:12,887 --> 00:00:14,221
Four different parts,

10
00:00:14,221 --> 00:00:15,301
working together.

11
00:00:15,851 --> 00:00:17,686
Today you draw the whole shop,

12
00:00:17,686 --> 00:00:18,481
part by part.

13
00:00:18,481 --> 00:00:21,784
Then you follow one single request through every part,

14
00:00:21,784 --> 00:00:23,680
and you find it in the diaries.

15
00:00:24,230 --> 00:00:27,345
And when something breaks, you will know which part to ask first.

16
00:00:29,395 --> 00:00:34,963
Let us draw CloudCart, one part at a time. First, the customer, and the browser they use.

17
00:00:35,513 --> 00:00:37,706
The first server is the web service,

18
00:00:37,706 --> 00:00:39,534
on port eight thousand eighty.

19
00:00:39,534 --> 00:00:41,849
Its only job is to hand over the page.

20
00:00:42,399 --> 00:00:43,822
The second is the API,

21
00:00:43,822 --> 00:00:45,245
on port five thousand.

22
00:00:45,245 --> 00:00:47,251
It holds the rules of the shop,

23
00:00:47,251 --> 00:00:50,420
and it is the only one allowed to touch the data.

24
00:00:50,970 --> 00:00:54,508
And behind the API sits one file: shop dot D B.

25
00:00:54,508 --> 00:00:56,089
That is the database.

26
00:00:56,089 --> 00:00:56,616
A file,

27
00:00:56,616 --> 00:00:57,594
not a server,

28
00:00:57,594 --> 00:00:58,949
so it has no port.

29
00:00:59,499 --> 00:01:00,950
Now trace one request.

30
00:01:00,950 --> 00:01:03,455
Step one: the customer opens the shop,

31
00:01:03,455 --> 00:01:06,752
and the browser asks the web service for the page.

32
00:01:07,302 --> 00:01:10,220
Step two: the web service sends the page back.

33
00:01:10,220 --> 00:01:12,313
The page carries a small program,

34
00:01:12,313 --> 00:01:14,406
and it knows where the API lives.

35
00:01:14,956 --> 00:01:19,778
Step three: that program, running in the browser, asks the API for the products.

36
00:01:20,328 --> 00:01:22,760
Step four: the API asks the database.

37
00:01:23,310 --> 00:01:26,143
Step five: the database returns the rows.

38
00:01:26,143 --> 00:01:29,045
Step six: the API turns them into jay son,

39
00:01:29,045 --> 00:01:31,118
and sends them to the browser.

40
00:01:31,668 --> 00:01:36,169
Step seven: the browser draws the product cards. The customer sees the shop.

41
00:01:36,719 --> 00:01:41,946
Seven steps, four parts. And one label, a request I D, can follow the whole way.

42
00:01:44,496 --> 00:01:47,611
Go into the shop. Type: CD, cloud cart.

43
00:01:48,161 --> 00:01:51,211
Start it. Type: dot slash start dot S H.

44
00:01:51,761 --> 00:01:53,205
A drawing is only a claim.

45
00:01:53,205 --> 00:01:55,481
Let us check it against the real machine.

46
00:01:55,481 --> 00:01:56,924
Which ports are listening?

47
00:01:57,474 --> 00:01:59,458
Type: S S, dash L T N.

48
00:02:01,508 --> 00:02:02,184
Two lines.

49
00:02:02,184 --> 00:02:04,213
Port five thousand is the API.

50
00:02:04,213 --> 00:02:07,324
Port eight thousand eighty is the web service.

51
00:02:07,324 --> 00:02:09,286
And no port for the database,

52
00:02:09,286 --> 00:02:11,044
because it is just a file.

53
00:02:11,594 --> 00:02:14,386
A second check: one answer from each layer.

54
00:02:14,386 --> 00:02:18,995
A small script called layers dot S H asks the web service for the page,

55
00:02:18,995 --> 00:02:20,618
and the API for the data.

56
00:02:21,168 --> 00:02:23,472
Type: dot slash layers dot S H.

57
00:02:25,522 --> 00:02:27,826
Web, two hundred. The page is served.

58
00:02:28,376 --> 00:02:33,411
API, two hundred. The data is served. Two layers, two answers, both healthy.

59
00:02:35,461 --> 00:02:38,576
Go into the shop. Type: CD, cloud cart.

60
00:02:39,126 --> 00:02:42,176
Start it. Type: dot slash start dot S H.

61
00:02:42,726 --> 00:02:44,395
Now we trace one request,

62
00:02:44,395 --> 00:02:44,995
for real.

63
00:02:44,995 --> 00:02:46,263
We give it a label,

64
00:02:46,263 --> 00:02:46,930
trace one,

65
00:02:46,930 --> 00:02:48,532
so we can find it later.

66
00:02:48,532 --> 00:02:51,068
Step one: the customer opens the page.

67
00:02:51,618 --> 00:02:52,405
Type: curl,

68
00:02:52,405 --> 00:02:52,905
dash s,

69
00:02:52,905 --> 00:02:53,978
dash capital H,

70
00:02:53,978 --> 00:02:54,694
in quotes,

71
00:02:54,694 --> 00:02:55,695
X request I D,

72
00:02:55,695 --> 00:02:56,124
colon,

73
00:02:56,124 --> 00:02:56,840
trace one,

74
00:02:56,840 --> 00:02:57,198
then,

75
00:02:57,198 --> 00:02:58,414
on the next line,

76
00:02:58,414 --> 00:02:59,201
local host,

77
00:02:59,201 --> 00:02:59,630
colon,

78
00:02:59,630 --> 00:03:01,204
eight thousand eighty,

79
00:03:01,204 --> 00:03:03,564
redirect to slash dev slash null.

80
00:03:05,914 --> 00:03:06,926
Nothing printed,

81
00:03:06,926 --> 00:03:08,888
because we threw the page away.

82
00:03:08,888 --> 00:03:12,367
We only wanted the web service to write its diary line.

83
00:03:12,367 --> 00:03:15,593
Step three: the page asks the API for the products,

84
00:03:15,593 --> 00:03:16,858
with the same label.

85
00:03:17,408 --> 00:03:18,243
Type: curl,

86
00:03:18,243 --> 00:03:18,774
dash s,

87
00:03:18,774 --> 00:03:19,912
dash capital H,

88
00:03:19,912 --> 00:03:20,671
in quotes,

89
00:03:20,671 --> 00:03:21,733
X request I D,

90
00:03:21,733 --> 00:03:22,188
colon,

91
00:03:22,188 --> 00:03:22,947
trace one,

92
00:03:22,947 --> 00:03:23,326
then,

93
00:03:23,326 --> 00:03:24,616
on the next line,

94
00:03:24,616 --> 00:03:25,450
local host,

95
00:03:25,450 --> 00:03:25,905
colon,

96
00:03:25,905 --> 00:03:26,968
five thousand,

97
00:03:26,968 --> 00:03:28,864
slash API slash products.

98
00:03:31,214 --> 00:03:33,952
Step six: the data comes back as jay son,

99
00:03:33,952 --> 00:03:35,621
a list of three products.

100
00:03:35,621 --> 00:03:38,425
That is what the browser turns into cards.

101
00:03:38,975 --> 00:03:40,082
Now the proof.

102
00:03:40,082 --> 00:03:42,216
Both services keep a diary.

103
00:03:42,216 --> 00:03:44,271
Search both for our label.

104
00:03:44,271 --> 00:03:45,141
Type: grep,

105
00:03:45,141 --> 00:03:45,931
trace one,

106
00:03:45,931 --> 00:03:46,880
web dot log,

107
00:03:46,880 --> 00:03:47,828
API dot log.

108
00:03:49,878 --> 00:03:53,612
First line: the web service. It served the page for trace one.

109
00:03:54,162 --> 00:03:55,657
Second line: the API.

110
00:03:55,657 --> 00:03:58,649
It served the data for the same trace one.

111
00:03:58,649 --> 00:03:59,361
One label,

112
00:03:59,361 --> 00:04:03,420
two diaries: we followed one request across two services.

113
00:04:04,470 --> 00:04:10,102
And the data itself lives in one place. Type: python three, show D B dot P Y.

114
00:04:12,152 --> 00:04:12,874
Three rows.

115
00:04:12,874 --> 00:04:14,120
The API read these,

116
00:04:14,120 --> 00:04:17,398
and turned them into the jay son the customer saw.

117
00:04:17,398 --> 00:04:20,152
That is the end of the road: the database.

118
00:04:22,202 --> 00:04:25,317
Go into the shop. Type: CD, cloud cart.

119
00:04:25,867 --> 00:04:28,917
Start it. Type: dot slash start dot S H.

120
00:04:29,467 --> 00:04:31,017
When the shop breaks,

121
00:04:31,017 --> 00:04:33,601
a customer only says: it is broken.

122
00:04:33,601 --> 00:04:35,963
Your job is to find which layer.

123
00:04:35,963 --> 00:04:36,184
So,

124
00:04:36,184 --> 00:04:37,291
ask each layer.

125
00:04:37,291 --> 00:04:39,579
Type: dot slash layers dot S H.

126
00:04:41,629 --> 00:04:47,283
Both two hundred. Healthy. Now we break one layer on purpose. We stop only the API.

127
00:04:47,833 --> 00:04:50,393
Type: dot slash API dot S H, stop.

128
00:04:51,943 --> 00:04:56,017
Ask each layer again. Type: dot slash layers dot S H.

129
00:04:58,067 --> 00:05:00,521
Web: still two hundred. The page loads.

130
00:05:01,071 --> 00:05:02,517
API: zero zero zero.

131
00:05:02,517 --> 00:05:03,964
Nobody is listening.

132
00:05:03,964 --> 00:05:07,146
The customer sees a page with an empty shop.

133
00:05:07,146 --> 00:05:09,967
And now you know exactly where to look.

134
00:05:10,517 --> 00:05:12,570
That is the skill: a symptom,

135
00:05:12,570 --> 00:05:14,907
then one question for each layer,

136
00:05:14,907 --> 00:05:18,234
and the first layer that fails is your suspect.

137
00:05:18,234 --> 00:05:19,651
Start the API again.

138
00:05:19,651 --> 00:05:21,633
Type: dot slash API dot S H,

139
00:05:21,633 --> 00:05:22,058
start.

140
00:05:23,608 --> 00:05:27,427
And ask once more. Type: dot slash layers dot S H.

141
00:05:29,477 --> 00:05:32,101
Both layers answer. The shop is whole again.

142
00:05:34,151 --> 00:05:37,308
Let us put it together: a map, a path, and a method.

143
00:05:37,858 --> 00:05:41,634
The map: a browser, a web service, an API, and a database.

144
00:05:42,184 --> 00:05:45,231
The path: the page comes from the web service,

145
00:05:45,231 --> 00:05:47,086
the data comes from the API,

146
00:05:47,086 --> 00:05:49,139
and the API reads the database.

147
00:05:49,689 --> 00:05:51,564
The label: one request I D,

148
00:05:51,564 --> 00:05:53,092
written in each diary,

149
00:05:53,092 --> 00:05:55,940
joins the pieces of one customer's visit.

150
00:05:56,490 --> 00:05:58,477
The method: when something breaks,

151
00:05:58,477 --> 00:06:00,464
start from what the customer sees,

152
00:06:00,464 --> 00:06:02,100
and ask one layer at a time.

153
00:06:02,650 --> 00:06:05,970
Page does not load: suspect the web service.

154
00:06:05,970 --> 00:06:09,290
Page loads but no products: suspect the API.

155
00:06:09,290 --> 00:06:12,912
API answers but not ready: suspect the database.

156
00:06:13,462 --> 00:06:18,859
And when it is slow, read the metrics. A diagram you can trace is a system you can fix.

157
00:06:20,909 --> 00:06:23,682
Your task, in your own Ubuntu virtual machine.

158
00:06:24,232 --> 00:06:26,868
The lab is lab seventy-four dot S H,

159
00:06:26,868 --> 00:06:30,602
in the academy slash lab folder of git hub dot com,

160
00:06:30,602 --> 00:06:32,066
slash it dash waves,

161
00:06:32,066 --> 00:06:33,750
slash dev ops dash A I.

162
00:06:33,750 --> 00:06:35,434
Install it like before,

163
00:06:35,434 --> 00:06:36,239
run lab up,

164
00:06:36,239 --> 00:06:39,827
and work inside slash opt slash lab seventy-four.

165
00:06:40,377 --> 00:06:44,068
One: list the listening ports, and save them in parts dot text.

166
00:06:44,618 --> 00:06:46,432
Two: with the shop healthy,

167
00:06:46,432 --> 00:06:50,868
run layers dot S H and save the output in layers dash up dot text.

168
00:06:51,418 --> 00:06:56,834
Three: send one request with the I D lab dash seventy-four to the web service,

169
00:06:56,834 --> 00:06:58,292
and again to the API.

170
00:06:58,292 --> 00:07:00,028
Then search both diaries,

171
00:07:00,028 --> 00:07:02,597
and save the lines in trace dot text.

172
00:07:03,147 --> 00:07:04,555
Four: stop the API,

173
00:07:04,555 --> 00:07:06,407
run layers dot S H again,

174
00:07:06,407 --> 00:07:10,038
and save the output in layers dash down dot text.

175
00:07:10,588 --> 00:07:12,221
Five: in answers dot text,

176
00:07:12,221 --> 00:07:14,231
write which part gives the page,

177
00:07:14,231 --> 00:07:15,864
which part gives the data,

178
00:07:15,864 --> 00:07:17,372
and where the rows live.

179
00:07:17,922 --> 00:07:23,447
Six: start the API again, so the shop is whole. Then run lab check. Six pass lines.

180
00:07:25,497 --> 00:07:27,481
Six points, and you need all six.

181
00:07:28,031 --> 00:07:29,866
The checker shows six pass lines.

182
00:07:30,416 --> 00:07:33,274
You can draw the four parts, and name each one's job.

183
00:07:33,824 --> 00:07:36,726
You can follow one request I D through two diaries.

184
00:07:37,276 --> 00:07:40,369
You can say which layer is broken from what the customer sees.

185
00:07:40,919 --> 00:07:43,522
You can explain why the database has no port.

186
00:07:44,072 --> 00:07:46,802
You ran lab down, and nothing is left listening.

187
00:07:47,352 --> 00:07:48,974
To pass, you need all six.

188
00:07:51,024 --> 00:07:53,861
Your turn, in your own Ubuntu virtual machine.

189
00:07:54,411 --> 00:07:56,630
One: install the lab, and run lab up.

190
00:07:57,180 --> 00:07:59,399
Two: list the ports, and ask each layer.

191
00:07:59,949 --> 00:08:04,258
Three: send a request with your own I D, and find it in both diaries.

192
00:08:04,808 --> 00:08:07,944
Four: stop the API, and ask each layer again.

193
00:08:08,494 --> 00:08:11,566
Five: write your answers, and start the API again.

194
00:08:12,116 --> 00:08:14,399
Six: run lab check, then lab down.

195
00:08:14,949 --> 00:08:16,783
Pause the video, and begin now.

196
00:08:32,333 --> 00:08:33,208
Quick check.

197
00:08:33,758 --> 00:08:36,851
Name the four parts of CloudCart, and what each one does.

198
00:08:37,401 --> 00:08:39,300
What does a request I D let you do?

199
00:08:39,850 --> 00:08:43,711
The page loads, but no products show. Which layer do you suspect?

200
00:08:44,261 --> 00:08:46,288
Why does the database have no port?

201
00:08:46,838 --> 00:08:49,081
Objective covered: M C zero eight,

202
00:08:49,081 --> 00:08:51,192
objective eight: draw CloudCart,

203
00:08:51,192 --> 00:08:53,238
and trace a request through it.

204
00:08:53,788 --> 00:08:55,857
Pause the video, and answer out loud.

205
00:09:06,407 --> 00:09:11,506
Next: the M C zero eight mastery lesson, where you fix a broken shop on your own.

206
00:09:12,056 --> 00:09:15,384
